        "Subsection 5.2.7 — Mapping Swap Proceeds and Mineral Revenues Across the Four Escrow Tranches. Desk 07's Conditional Escrow Waterfall partitions the pooled capital—both conservation-funded debt-relief proceeds and future escrow-assigned mineral royalty receivables—across default tranche weights 25, 25, 30, and 20, linking release deterministically to upstream bus signals rather than ministerial drawdown memos. Look carefully at what each tranche finances and enforces in a sovereign restructuring carrying clouded mining titles. Tranche 1 (Mobilisation, 25 per cent) releases strictly once an independent external verifier sits on the Verification Ledger; those initial funds finance the independent conservation trust secretariat and pay a neutral forensic procurement and legal audit team to examine every contested mineral concession granted under prior regimes before a single dollar of ore revenue enters creditor collateral.",
